        "What does the business idiom 'an across-the-board 20% price increase' mean in Section 2?|Applying a uniform 20% price increase to every single product in the catalogue without exception|Writing prices on a wooden board in the office|Increasing prices only for foreign buyers|Lowering prices by 20%",
        "Why does the Strategy Head advise AGAINST a flat 20% price hike?|Because mid-market retail clients are highly price-sensitive, so a sudden 20% hike would cause a 15% drop in sales volume and lose shelf space to competitors|Because price increases are illegal in January|Because printing new catalogues is too expensive|Because the company has no competitors",
        "How does the proposed 'nearshoring' strategy in Section 3 reduce the 'net landed cost' by 8% even though Turkish and Polish factory prices are 5% higher than Asian prices?|Because overland rail and truck freight costs from Turkey and Poland are 60% lower than sea containers from Asia, and shorter transit times halve safety-stock requirements|Because Turkish and Polish steel weighs less|Because the government pays for the trucks|Because there is no quality inspection needed",
