        "What is 'Total Factor Productivity' (TFP) in macroeconomics?|The efficiency, management quality, and technological sophistication with which capital and labour are combined to produce higher-value output|The total number of hours worked in a year|The total weight of goods exported by ship|The sum of all bank deposits",
        "How did East Asian economies like South Korea and Taiwan successfully escape the middle-income trap in the late 20th century (Section 3)?|By executing a deliberate pivot from 'imitation' to 'indigenous innovation' — investing over 3% of GDP in R&D and linking university engineering faculties directly with export-oriented industrial clusters|By keeping wages as low as possible forever|By exporting only agricultural fruit and timber|By abolishing all universities",
